CRDs in Kubernetes: Extend the API Your Way

Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs) let you create your own Kubernetes resource types—just like Pods or Services.

What They Do:
- Extend the Kubernetes API
- Let you define custom objects (e.g., MyApp, Database)
- Allow controllers/operators to manage them like native resources

When built-in resources aren’t enough, CRDs help you model and manage custom infrastructure needs.
